**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests`

**How to implement.** A kit snapshots every library version it references, closure and built-ins included, and the library pins each (001 §E 'Library closure snapshot: every library version the kit references is copied into library/ when first referenced, built-ins included, because the receiver may run another catalogue version'; 001 §C 'A version becomes Pinned — a one-way flag — when a kit first references it'; the S4.2 brief: its entry file is written byte-identical to `library/<id>@v<n>.<kind>-json`, and the version is PINNED in the database (S2.2)). New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitLibrary.fs`: `module KitLibrary` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `CatalogueImport.fs` (step 37), because it reads the import seam: one `<Compile>` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` and no comment. It opens `Kit`, `KitFolders`, `LibraryEntryFiles` and `CatalogueImport`. Each type and member has a doc of one to three lines citing spec 0050 S4.2. (1) `KitLibraryError`, an `*Error` union: `KitLibraryKitErr of KitError`, `KitLibraryImportErr of CatalogueImportError`, and `UnheldEntryErr of reason : string`, a reference that neither the library nor the kit's snapshots hold, naming its `describe`. `member this.describe : string` renders each in step 39's form, a wrapped error by its own `describe`. (2) `[<ReferenceEquality>] KitLibraryContext = { kit : KitContext; imports : CatalogueImportContext }`: one opened kit (step 131) and the library's import seam (step 94), the `*Context` convention. (3) `member this.snapshotReferences (references : EntryReference list) : Result<LibraryVersionRef list, KitLibraryError>` works in this order. Under `ReadOnlyKitAccess` it answers `KitLibraryKitErr (KitReadOnlyErr "snapshotReferences")`, reading, pinning and writing nothing. It lists the kit's snapshots (`kit.proxy.listSnapshots`, step 138). It resolves each reference to one envelope. `EntryVersionReference r` is the kit's own snapshot of `r` when it holds one, and otherwise `imports.proxy.tryHeldEnvelope r.entryId r.version` (step 105). `EntryLatestReference id` is `imports.proxy.tryLatestEnvelope id` (step 116), and otherwise the kit's highest-version snapshot of `id`. Neither is `UnheldEntryErr`. It walks each resolved envelope and then its `content.references` (step 137), depth first and in order, so a sample brings its material versions and each material its category, and every version is visited once. Each visited version the kit holds no snapshot of is pinned through `imports.proxy.pinEntryVersion` and then written through `kit.proxy.writeSnapshot` (step 138). It pins first, as `exportEntry` (step 116) pins before it writes, so a written snapshot always names a pinned version. A version the kit already holds is neither rewritten nor pinned, even when the library's copy of that version differs: the kit keeps its snapshot (001 §E). The answer is every version written, in visit order. The first failure stops it, and what it wrote stays, so calling it again completes the work. Its callers are the writers of kit content that binds library versions: the kit's experiment and setup files pass what they bind (an experiment's `libraryReferences`, step 137) once a constructor session holds a kit (S4.3), as S7.1's items and S11.5's promotion do in their sections. No cache, retry or option is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs`, `module KitLibraryTests`, appended at the end of the compile list of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj` with no comment. Its library is `BuiltinCatalogue.freshStores ()` (step 94), and its import context is `CatalogueImportContext.create` over that seam with `pinEntryVersion` wrapped by a test-local recorder of every pin, in order. Its kit is `KitProxy.createInMemory` over a fresh `InMemoryKitFolder`, initialised with a test-local kit file and opened through `KitContext.openKit` with a stepping clock. `referencing a sample snapshots it with its materials and their categories, each once, and pins each`: `snapshotReferences` of the `EntryVersionReference` of `SampleIds.multilayerQwId` at version 1 answers, in order, the sample's version, then each of its materials followed by that material's category, each version once. `listSnapshots` answers exactly their catalogue envelopes, and the recorder holds the same versions in the same order. `referencing a version the kit already holds writes and pins nothing`: the same call again answers `Ok []`, records no pin and leaves `paths` unchanged. `a preset referenced by its id snapshots the library's latest version`: the `EntryLatestReference` of the GUID of `PresetIds.source600` answers that source's version 1 and writes its envelope. `a version the kit holds is kept even when the library's differs, and one the library lacks resolves from the kit`: with the kit already holding a sealed copy of Silicon at version 1 whose description differs, a reference to Silicon at version 1 answers `[]`, records no pin and leaves that copy as the kit's snapshot. With the kit holding the snapshot of a test-local user material that the library does not hold, a reference to it at its version answers `[]`. `a reference neither the library nor the kit holds is UnheldEntryErr and writes nothing`: a reference to a test-local GUID answers `UnheldEntryErr` naming it, and the recorder and `paths` are unchanged. `a read-only kit refuses to snapshot and pins nothing`: over a context opened with `ReadOnlyKitAccess`, the call answers `KitLibraryKitErr (KitReadOnlyErr _)`, the recorder is empty and `paths` is unchanged. `a snapshot pins its version rows in the library database` runs over SQLite: with the import seam `CatalogueImportProxy.createInDatabase` (step 95) of `BuiltinCatalogue.freshLibraryDatabase ()` (step 67), disposed by the fact, after the multilayer sample's reference every answered version reads `VersionPinned` through `run` and `tryStoredVersion`, and every other catalogue version stays `VersionUnpinned`. `every kit library error renders its condition and its payload`: each case, over a distinct test-local reason or a wrapped `KitIoErr` or `ImportRejectedErr`, renders a distinct text that holds its reason or the wrapped error's `describe`.

**Acceptance.** After snapshotting lands, `KitLibraryContext.snapshotReferences` MUST write every referenced version and its closure once into `library/`, pin each in the library before writing it, keep a version the kit already holds, and refuse under a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `referencing a sample snapshots it with its materials and their categories, each once, and pins each`, `referencing a version the kit already holds writes and pins nothing`, `a preset referenced by its id snapshots the library's latest version`, `a version the kit holds is kept even when the library's differs, and one the library lacks resolves from the kit`, `a reference neither the library nor the kit holds is UnheldEntryErr and writes nothing`, `a read-only kit refuses to snapshot and pins nothing`, `a snapshot pins its version rows in the library database`, `every kit library error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 8; and build, elevation and the eleven s16 invariants MUST pass.
